# IoT Cache Replacement Prediction

A machine learning project for predicting cache replacement decisions using IoT data characteristics.

## Project Overview

This project explores a binary classification approach for predicting whether an IoT data item should be replaced from a cache.

The project is implemented using Python and PyTorch.

## Dataset

The dataset contains 3,000 synthetic samples.

Features:

* Recency
* Access Count
* Size
* Remaining TTL
* Data Type

Target:

* `replacement = 0` → Keep the item
* `replacement = 1` → Replace the item

## Model

The initial model is a feed-forward neural network implemented with PyTorch.

Architecture:

```text
5 Input Features
      ↓
Linear(5 → 16)
      ↓
ReLU
      ↓
Linear(16 → 8)
      ↓
ReLU
      ↓
Linear(8 → 1)
```

The model uses:

* `BCEWithLogitsLoss`
* Adam optimizer
* Binary classification

## Initial Results

The initial neural network achieved:

* Accuracy: 71.17%
* Class 0 Recall: 0.32
* Class 1 Recall: 0.91

These results are part of the initial version of the project and further experiments will be performed.

